    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "letters-027",
    "front": "ἀ",
    "back": "Smooth breathing = no /h/; the vowel is read plain: ἀ- = 'a-'. Every initial vowel takes a breathing: ἀγρός 'field'.",
    "chapter": 4,
    "card_type": "Diacritic",
    "pos": "diacritic",
    "tags": [
      "letters",
      "chapter-4",
      "breathing"
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "letters-028",
    "front": "ά",
    "back": "Acute accent: pitch rose on this syllable (a pitch accent; read as stress today): ἀγρός 'field'.",
    "chapter": 4,
    "card_type": "Diacritic",
    "pos": "diacritic",
    "tags": [
      "letters",
      "chapter-4",
      "accent"
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "letters-029",
    "front": "ὰ",
    "back": "Grave accent: a final acute drops to grave when another word follows: καλὸν καὶ ἀγαθόν 'good and beautiful'.",
    "chapter": 4,
    "card_type": "Diacritic",
    "pos": "diacritic",
    "tags": [
